reports/tmp-*/
# Raw EMODnet bathymetry transects: 25 MB of third-party floats, 1.000 samples
# per beach, re-fetchable by re-running scripts/auditWaterDepth.mjs (~25 min).
# The findings live in the report JSON next to it, which IS tracked — the same
# split as reports/terrain/, whose cache is only 131 KB and so was kept.
reports/water-depth/emodnet-profile-cache.json
reports/water-depth/run-national.log
OUT.txt

# Capacitor / native app store packaging
# Generated icon/splash sources (reproducible via `npm run native:assets`)
cap-assets/
store-assets/
# Android signing keys — NEVER commit; keep an offline backup
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
# iOS native project pods (added later on macOS)
ios/App/Pods/

# Internal, non-shippable, or sensitive-in-a-public-repo files
# (repo is public — keep competitive strategy and the machine-specific MCP
# config out of git so they never get pushed by accident)
.mcp.json
docs/competitor-strategy.md
# reports/snapshots/ and data/analytics/ WERE gitignored for the same reason —
# un-ignored 30/07/2026 on purpose: that made them the single point of failure
# ("lives on one laptop, no copy anywhere", see docs/team/12-growth-analytics.md
# risk #1). Search Console/GA numbers are not competitively sensitive the way
# docs/team/ is; tracking them is the fix, not a new leak.
# docs/team/ — the 17 role docs. Same reason as the two lines above: they hold the
# negotiating position against a named competitor, monetization thresholds, the legal
# history, and a concentrated map of our own weak points. Useful internally, not for a
# public repo. They live on disk and the calmbeach-team skill reads them normally —
# keep a copy outside the repo (Drive/OneDrive), since git is no longer the backup.
docs/team/

# Baked SQLite database — a build artifact regenerated from the canonical JSON
# via `npm run build:sqlite`; not committed (binary, 1.7MB).
public/data/beaches.sqlite
public/data/beaches.sqlite-wal
public/data/beaches.sqlite-shm

# Build/analysis artifact — whole-country SQLite, never served (see sqlite-verdict)
data/derived/

# Local Netlify folder
.netlify

# Netlify edge bootstrap lockfile — regenerated by `netlify dev`, never read by the build
# (netlify.toml declares no edge_functions; only netlify/functions, which are Node).
deno.lock

# Ενδιάμεσο αρχείο του snapshot: χωρίς ημερομηνία στο όνομα, ξαναγράφεται κάθε
# φορά, 700 KB. Τα dated reports/snapshots/*.json|*.md ΕΙΝΑΙ tracked (η μέτρηση
# GSC είναι το ιστορικό)· αυτό εδώ είναι μόνο η πρώτη ύλη τους.
reports/snapshots/_raw-queries.json
